values ('c8d9e0f1-2a3b-4c13-8d52-6e7f8a9b0c03', 'food-safety-and-sanitation', 'Food Safety and Sanitation', 'This course introduces the science, law, systems, and managerial practices used to prevent foodborne illness and protect food in hospitality operations. Students identify biological, chemical, physical, and allergen hazards; apply employee health and hygiene controls; manage time and temperature; protect food through purchasing, receiving, storage, preparation, cooking, cooling, holding, service, delivery, and catering; design cleaning, sanitation, pest, facility, and utility controls; build HACCP and active-managerial-control systems; interpret inspection findings; strengthen food-safety culture; and respond to complaints, outbreaks, recalls, and emergencies. Applied laboratories and case exercises prepare students for an accredited food protection manager examination while emphasizing that certification complements—not replaces—competent daily management.');

